  "text_md": "and\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nTo calculate the curve-averaged value of the basis function of the p 2 polynomial in Eq. 19, the following integral needs to be calculated\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nwhere θ 0 = arctan( √ ϕ 0 ϕ 2 ϕ 1 ), θ 1 = arctan( √ ϕ 0 ϕ 2 (1 + ϕ 1 )). If p is an odd integer p = 2 k +1,\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nIf p is an even integer p = 2 k ,\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n## B. Quadratic integral on curved triangle\n\nThe isoparametric transformations of the quadratic triangular cell Eq. 30 is\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nwhere a 0 = 4( x 0 + x 1 -2 x 3 ) , a 1 = 4( x 0 -x 3 + x 4 -x 5 ) , a 2 = -3 x 0 -x 1 + 4 x 3 , a 3 = 4( x 0 -x 3 + x 4 -x 5 ) , a 4 = 4( x 0 + x 2 -2 x 5 ) , a 5 = -3 x 0 -x 2 +4 x 5 , b 0 = 4( y 0 + y 1 -2 y 3 ) , b 1 = 4( y 0 -y 3 + y 4 -y 5 ) , b 2 = -3 y 0 -y 1 +4 y 3 , b 3 = 4( y 0 -y 3 + y 4 -y 5 ) , b 4 = 4( y 0 + y 2 -2 y 5 ) , b 5 = -3 y 0 -y 2 +4 y 5 .",
